Branch: master&lt;br/&gt;
Current Patch Set: 1&lt;br/&gt;
Commit: bf1f1f6ad661869e1e0cb45f5a27a03ffb7df609&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="501385" author="adilger" created="Thu, 10 Sep 2026 22:16:37 +0000"  >
&lt;p&gt;I think the most important part of any such fix is to not leave uninitialized fields in the layout, for any field, whether it is used or not. Otherwise we can never safely use those fields in the future.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Normally we zero all memory in Lustre before use, so I don&apos;t know where the garbage is coming from (userspace or the kernel, or both), but I think that is the first order issue to understand and fix.  Running this against my home filesystem it looks like I have bad timestamps dating back to files &lt;em&gt;created&lt;/em&gt; in 2021, which would likely mean 2.14.x or so? So it isn&apos;t a newly-introduced problem, just that we never printed this field before.  &lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;It probably makes sense to verify the &lt;tt&gt;lcme_time_and_id&lt;/tt&gt; field for every layout read:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul class=&quot;alternate&quot; type=&quot;square&quot;&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;consider it garbage and zero it if before 2010 or more than 1 year in the future&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;this would become permanent if the layout is written (e.g. mirrored or migrated)&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;set the timestamp for all mirrors when they are resync&apos;d (regardless of &lt;tt&gt;NOSYNC&lt;/tt&gt; flag) so we know when they were last updated&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
</comment>
                            <comment id="501579" author="JIRAUSER19288" created="Tue, 15 Sep 2026 17:00:37 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;(Apologies, I seem to not have sent my response...)&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;That sounds reasonable. I&apos;m working on updating the patch.&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="501585" author="gerrit" created="Tue, 15 Sep 2026 21:11:08 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;&quot;Marc Vef &amp;lt;mvef@whamcloud.com&amp;gt;&quot; uploaded a new patch: &lt;a href=&quot;https://review.whamcloud.com/c/fs/lustre-release/+/68932&quot; class=&quot;external-link&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot;&gt;https://review.whamcloud.com/c/fs/lustre-release/+/68932&lt;/a&gt;&lt;br/&gt;
Subject: &lt;a href=&quot;https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-20718&quot; title=&quot;Interop sanity-pfl test_18: Add component to /mnt/lustre/f18.sanity-pfl-1 failed 3 &quot; class=&quot;issue-link&quot; data-issue-key=&quot;LU-20718&quot;&gt;LU-20718&lt;/a&gt; lod: scrub stale EC fields from old layouts&lt;br/&gt;
Project: fs/lustre-release&lt;br/&gt;
Branch: master&lt;br/&gt;
Current Patch Set: 1&lt;br/&gt;
Commit: e4744910e5ce3bce6a386bd3d248d4c28d965c60&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="501586" author="JIRAUSER19288" created="Tue, 15 Sep 2026 21:18:33 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;I split &lt;a href=&quot;https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-20718&quot; title=&quot;Interop sanity-pfl test_18: Add component to /mnt/lustre/f18.sanity-pfl-1 failed 3 &quot; class=&quot;issue-link&quot; data-issue-key=&quot;LU-20718&quot;&gt;LU-20718&lt;/a&gt; and &lt;a href=&quot;https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-20623&quot; title=&quot;interop sanity test_27D: llapi_layout_test test30 test37 failed&quot; class=&quot;issue-link&quot; data-issue-key=&quot;LU-20623&quot;&gt;&lt;del&gt;LU-20623&lt;/del&gt;&lt;/a&gt; into three patches because there are separate issues in different parts of the code.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ol&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;llapi patch on &lt;a href=&quot;https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-20623&quot; title=&quot;interop sanity test_27D: llapi_layout_test test30 test37 failed&quot; class=&quot;issue-link&quot; data-issue-key=&quot;LU-20623&quot;&gt;&lt;del&gt;LU-20623&lt;/del&gt;&lt;/a&gt;. This should fix the specific issues seen during interop on 27D as you outlined in the ticket: &lt;a href=&quot;https://review.whamcloud.com/c/fs/lustre-release/+/68931&quot; class=&quot;external-link&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot;&gt;https://review.whamcloud.com/c/fs/lustre-release/+/68931&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;llapi patch on &lt;a href=&quot;https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-20718&quot; title=&quot;Interop sanity-pfl test_18: Add component to /mnt/lustre/f18.sanity-pfl-1 failed 3 &quot; class=&quot;issue-link&quot; data-issue-key=&quot;LU-20718&quot;&gt;LU-20718&lt;/a&gt;. This is the current patch but updated. Ignores stale EC fields from old servers and scrubs the EC fields on data components that are not EC protected. This should &quot;fix&quot; the interop issue for this ticket: &lt;a href=&quot;https://review.whamcloud.com/c/fs/lustre-release/+/68747&quot; class=&quot;external-link&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot;&gt;https://review.whamcloud.com/c/fs/lustre-release/+/68747&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;lod kernel side as part of &lt;a href=&quot;https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-20718&quot; title=&quot;Interop sanity-pfl test_18: Add component to /mnt/lustre/f18.sanity-pfl-1 failed 3 &quot; class=&quot;issue-link&quot; data-issue-key=&quot;LU-20718&quot;&gt;LU-20718&lt;/a&gt;. This zeroes the EA before packing it so no field is ever written uninitialized. And wherever this is parsed, clear a timestamp outside a plausible range. In addition, scrub the fields similar to the second patch. The layout is therefore &quot;repaired&quot; next time it is written. The same scrub is applied to the EA returned by &lt;tt&gt;lod_xattr_get()&lt;/tt&gt;, so clients never see the stale bytes in the first place, complimenting 2: &lt;a href=&quot;https://review.whamcloud.com/c/fs/lustre-release/+/68932&quot; class=&quot;external-link&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot;&gt;https://review.whamcloud.com/c/fs/lustre-release/+/68932&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;


&lt;p&gt;Patches that are currently stuck because interop fails can rebase on 2. to get the fixes for both issues.&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
